      "side": 1,
      "message": "Existing issue: The `reinterpret_cast` here, dereferencing a raw `uint8_t` array as a struct pointer, can be dangerous. It violates standard C++ Strict Aliasing rules (undefined behavior) and could cause alignment faults on architectures that strictly enforce it (like Cortex-M0). Since an HCI command parameter length is always the 4th byte of the H4 packet, accessing `h4Buf[3]` or using `h4Buf[1 + offsetof(struct bt_hci_cmd_hdr, param_len)]` would avoid casting entirely and satisfy compiler standards safely.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 45,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 45,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "bacf570e2a00e37e4e6fd2c285a334cd6d026eda",
